  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Literature task: \<langle\>issue URL\<rangle\>

    <item>Source revision: \<langle\>pinned Lean revision\<rangle\>

    <item>Status: \<langle\>lead / source checked / independently accepted /
    stale\<rangle\>

    <item>Contributor and agent assistance: \<langle\>accounts and
    tools\<rangle\>

    <item>Independent review: \<langle\>reviewer, reviewed commit, and review
    link; pending until checked\<rangle\>
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Result to be used><label|result-to-be-used>

  \<langle\>The exact version needed, with hypotheses and conclusion in the
  project's notation.\<rangle\>

  <section|Mathematical reference><label|mathematical-reference>

  \<langle\>Author, title, edition/version/year, theorem/section/page, and
  stable link or DOI where available. State whether the actual source
  statement has been inspected.\<rangle\>

  <section|Match to the formalisation><label|match-to-the-formalisation>

  \<langle\>Relevant fully qualified declarations and source paths. Compare
  definitions, quantifiers, hypotheses, and conventions. Identify any
  differences or extra steps.\<rangle\>

  <section|Application and remaining proof
  obligations><label|application-and-remaining-proof-obligations>

  \<langle\>What each consuming proof must check; extensions requiring proof;
  known uses.\<rangle\>

  <section|Search and unresolved questions><label|search-and-unresolved-questions>

  \<langle\>Useful sources/queries checked, unsuccessful leads worth
  recording, and gaps. Do not infer novelty from an unsuccessful
  search.\<rangle\>
